    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="1088" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/11–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consulate General at Batavia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-18T12:00:00-05:00">November 18,
                            1947—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>316. No. 19 for Graham. Reurtel 25<anchor n="48" xml:id="d868-f1"/> Dept’s views
                    re question withdrawal forces follow: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Penultimate para resolution Nov 1 does not require any
                            withdrawals.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Last para resolution Nov 1 contemplates parties may agree to
                            withdrawals as part workable arrangement to implement cease fire.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>
                            GOC may work out with parties such an
                            arrangement.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Dept in general agreement with other views urtel 25 except we consider proper meaning “occupied” (urtel para 6<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) is
                    “control” and prefer alternative definition “control” contained urtel para 6(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>).</p>
                <p>For your info last para resolution Nov 1
                    proposed in subcom by Belgian representative SC
                    with concurrence Netherlands Representative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
